            "title": "Multi-config path object now constructed before logging exists",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/hexo/index.js",
            "line": 37,
            "explanation": "`new MultiConfigPath(this)` is invoked before `this.log` is initialized, but `multi_config_path.js` immediately dereferences `ctx.log` and calls `log.w()`/`log.i()`. Passing any `--config` value that hits the multi-file branch now throws a TypeError during Hexo construction instead of returning a config path.",
            "suggestion": "Initialize `this.log` before creating the multi-config path helper, or defer creating the helper until after `this.log = logger(this.env)` is assigned.",
            "failureAfterChange": "`new Hexo('/site', {config: '_config.yml,_config.prod.yml'})` crashes with `Cannot read property 'w' of undefined` when `multiConfigPath()` tries to warn about missing files.",
